CORE
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract foo _ --enforce-contract foo
^EXIT=6$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*Contract enforcement cannot be applied to a binary that has already been instrumented by the DFCC pipeline.*$
^.*Only one DFCC pass per binary is supported.*$
--
^.*VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL.*$
This test enforces a contract on foo under the DFCC pipeline, then runs a
plain (non-DFCC) --enforce-contract foo on the resulting binary. The
second invocation must fail with a clean error: without the cross-mode
guard the non-DFCC path tripped an invariant (abort) on the already
DFCC-instrumented binary.
